    {
      "id": "W7225193169",
      "doi": "10.1515/joc-2026-0505",
      "title": "Performance evaluation of DNN–LSTM–based optical communication monitoring for joint failure diagnosis and physical-layer attack detection",
      "authors": [
        "Shayma Wail Nourildean",
        "Thamer M. Jamel"
      ],
      "year": 2026,
      "venue": "Journal of Optical Communications",
      "venue_abbr": "J. Opt. Commun.",
      "rank_label": "未匹配 CIE 2023",
      "keywords": [
        "optical performance monitoring",
        "bit error rate",
        "physical layer security"
      ],
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.1515/joc-2026-0505",
      "cited_by_count": 0,
      "importance": 1,
      "score_basis": {},
      "role": "root",
      "reading_url": "items/4954c5a0-4400-4cbb-a9c6-253fb6d43b3a.html",
      "summary": "研究提出按类别优化验证集融合权重的DNN–LSTM框架，识别正常运行、三类光故障及三类物理层攻击。攻击场景依据光学测量并施加物理约束构建，误码率由传输质量模型估算。在包含910,000个样本的平衡数据集上开展评估，其中独立测试集含210,000个样本；准确率为91.190%，宏F1为91.056%。光故障与物理层攻击的宏召回率分别为98.468%和80.553%。相较固定权重融合，宏F1由90.819%提升至91.056%。",
      "summary_basis": "本站解读 · abstract-only"
    },
